    {
      "id": "n5-u06-g02",
      "title": "な-adjectives — \"is quiet\", \"isn't quiet\"",
      "pattern": "N は な-adj です / な-adj じゃありません",
      "meaning": "N is (not) adj",
      "explanation": "な-adjectives are the second kind of adjective, like 静か (quiet) and 親切 (kind). At the end of a sentence they act just like nouns: add です to say \"is\", and じゃありません to say \"is not\". You do not add な here — the な only shows up when the adjective comes right before a noun (next lesson). Be careful: きれい and 有名 end in い, but they are な-adjectives.",
      "notes": [
        "きれい (pretty) and 有名 (famous) are な-adjectives, so the negative is きれいじゃありません, never きれくないです.",
        "ではありません is a more formal version of じゃありません."
      ],
      "examples": [
