      "meaning": "an adj N",
      "explanation": "To describe a noun directly, put the adjective in front of it, just like English. い-adjectives go straight in front with their い: 新しい時計 (a new watch). な-adjectives need な between the adjective and the noun: 静かな町 (a quiet town). That little な is how these adjectives got their name.",
